"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.6.1.stable.official [14d19694e]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA T1000 8GB (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8142) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-14700 (28 threads) - 47.69 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI've recently started working with root bone motion in animated characters.  I've noticed that on a GLB file I exported from Blender that the imported version in Godot is incorrectly swapping the Y and Z axes when I call `animation_tree.get_root_motion_rotation()`.  I need to manually swap them to fix the returned quaternion.\n\nI'm pretty sure the exported file has correct root motion since it displays with proper root motion in various viewers I've tried.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun the attached project.  If you select the swimmer character in the editor and toggle the `Correct Root Rotation` property, you can see the applied root motion animation both with and without the correction.\n\nIn the uncorrected version, the swimmer will spin about its local Z axis.  In the corrected version, it spins around the local Y axis.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[swimmer_turn_root.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25848696/swimmer_turn_root.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/